@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+# Billing
+
+Subscription billing: plans sold monthly or annually, subscriptions to them, and the invoices they produce.
+
+## Language
+
+### Selling and renewing
+
+**Plan**:
+A sellable offering with one list price per interval.
+_Avoid_: Product, tier, package
+
+**Interval**:
+How often a subscription is billed: monthly or annually.
+_Avoid_: Billing cycle, frequency, term
+
+**Period**:
+The span of days a subscription has paid for (or, while trialing, the free trial), from its start up to but not including its end.
+_Avoid_: Cycle, term
+
+**Retired plan**:
+A plan that can no longer be sold; customers already on it keep renewing at its price.
+_Avoid_: Deprecated plan, archived plan
+
+### Plan changes
+
+**Plan change**:
+A customer moving their existing subscription to a different plan, a different interval, or both, without cancelling it.
+_Avoid_: Switch, migration, resubscribe
+
+**Upgrade**:
+A plan change to a plan with a higher monthly list price, whatever interval the customer is on; it takes effect the day it is requested, prorated at the current interval's prices.
+_Avoid_: Immediate change
+
+**Downgrade**:
+A plan change to a plan with a lower monthly list price; it waits for the end of the current period, and nothing is billed or refunded when it is requested.
+_Avoid_: Deferred change
+
+**Lateral change**:
+A plan change to a different plan with the same monthly list price; it takes effect the day it is requested.
+
+**Interval switch**:
+A change of interval, monthly to annual or back; it is neither an upgrade nor a downgrade, always waits for the end of the current period, and is never prorated.
+_Avoid_: Interval upgrade, interval downgrade
+
+**Scheduled change**:
+The downgrade and/or interval switch a subscription will take on at its next renewal; at most one exists per subscription, and each new plan change request replaces it.
+_Avoid_: Pending change, queued change
+
+**Proration**:
+Splitting the current period at the day of an upgrade so that every day is paid for exactly once, on the old terms before it and on the new terms from it.
+
+**Proration credit**:
+The negative amount, on an upgrade's invoice, for the unused days of the current period on the old terms; it is never paid out, so when it is at least the proration charge nothing is billed.
+_Avoid_: Refund
+
+**Proration charge**:
+The amount, on an upgrade's invoice, for the new terms from the day of the upgrade.
