new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e608265
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0001-plan-changes-without-refunds.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# Plan changes never pay money out, and interval switches wait for the renewal
+
+Billing has no customer credit balance and no refund path (`cancel` refunds nothing), so plan changes are designed never to owe the customer money. Only an upgrade or lateral change (a different plan, compared by monthly list price) applies mid-period, prorated by calendar day at the current interval's prices. If its proration credit is at least the proration charge, nothing is billed and the credit is forfeited. Downgrades and interval switches, monthly to annual included, wait for the end of the current period and are never prorated. A request that combines an upgrade with an interval switch is split: the upgrade applies now and the switch is scheduled.
+
+## Considered Options
+
+- **Prorate interval switches immediately** (start a new period of the new interval today, credit the unused old period). Rejected: annual to monthly would almost always owe the customer money, and treating monthly to annual differently from annual to monthly would make the rules harder for support to explain.
+- **Issue negative-total invoices (refunds) or carry a credit balance** for downgrades and over-credited changes. Rejected: either one adds a money-out path the domain doesn't have, just for plan changes.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A customer switching from monthly to annual keeps paying monthly until their current month ends.
+- On an annual subscription, an upgrade to a plan with a discounted annual price can be applied with nothing billed, and the customer doesn't get the difference back.
